---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Projects & Case Studies — Pedro Ivo Vasconcelos | Data Platforms & Applied AI" description="Engineered systems, data platforms, deterministic simulators, and WebGL architectures by Pedro Ivo Vasconcelos.">
  <main id="conteudo" class="container" style="padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 5rem;">
    <div class="section-heading" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Engineered Systems</p>
      <h1>Projects & Technical Case Studies</h1>
      <p>
        Architectures designed for resilience, mathematical determinism, high throughput, and zero-compromise reliability.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3rem;">
      <!-- Project 1: Quantorin AI -->
      <article class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--accent);">Control Plane & AI Systems</span>
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; margin-top: 0.25rem;">Quantorin AI</h2>
            <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--text);">Autonomous Agent Orchestration & Specialist Control Plane</p>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center;">
            <a href="https://quantorin.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem; font-size: 0.85rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: var(--surface-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line);">Live Platform ↗</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/pedroivovasconcelos/Quantorin" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem; font-size: 0.85rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: var(--surface-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line);">GitHub ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p style="color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          Enterprise agent mesh and evaluation control plane running on Next.js 16 with React 19 Turbopack. Integrates 80 autonomous modules and 30 guild specialists across isolated ACP (Agent Communication Protocol) channels with immutable sanitization receipts.
        </p>

        <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);">
          <strong style="display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text);">Architecture & Engineering Highlights:</strong>
          <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-soft); margin: 0;">
            <li><strong>Fail-Closed Gatekeeper:</strong> Strict isolation preventing hallucinated actions or out-of-boundary tool calls.</li>
            <li><strong>Model Context Protocol (MCP):</strong> Native transport integration for real-time tooling, database introspection, and multi-model consensus.</li>
            <li><strong>Static Performance Audit:</strong> 100/100 Lighthouse performance baseline, zero-layout-shift responsive HUD.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <span class="tag">Next.js 16</span>
          <span class="tag">React 19</span>
          <span class="tag">TypeScript</span>
          <span class="tag">Model Context Protocol</span>
          <span class="tag">Turbopack</span>
          <span class="tag">Vercel Edge</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Project 2: Work & Slop Games -->
      <article class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--accent);">3D Graphics & Game Engine</span>
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; margin-top: 0.25rem;">Work & Slop Games</h2>
            <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--text);">WebGL 3D Arcade Platform & Isolated Game SDK</p>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center;">
            <a href="https://workslop-games.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem; font-size: 0.85rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: var(--surface-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line);">Live Games ↗</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/pedroivovasconcelos/Quantorin/tree/main/apps/workslop-games" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem; font-size: 0.85rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: var(--surface-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line);">GitHub ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p style="color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          Canonical browser gaming ecosystem built with Babylon.js 9.20.0 and WebGL. Features 11 playable titles, seamless full-bleed 100dvh rendering, in-game floating HUDs, and an isolated postMessage communication protocol ensuring zero security leakage between host and game runtimes.
        </p>

        <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);">
          <strong style="display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text);">Architecture & Engineering Highlights:</strong>
          <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-soft); margin: 0;">
            <li><strong>259+ Automated Unit & Integration Tests:</strong> 100% test pass rate covering physics step loops, drift slip-angles, and state machines.</li>
            <li><strong>Continuous Level-of-Detail (LOD):</strong> Dynamic geometry culling and texture LOD maintaining steady 60 FPS on both mobile and desktop.</li>
            <li><strong>Full-Bleed Responsive Viewport:</strong> Dynamic auto-hide single-row header and touch-optimized virtual joysticks for mobile landscape play.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <span class="tag">Babylon.js 9.20</span>
          <span class="tag">WebGL / WebGPU</span>
          <span class="tag">TypeScript</span>
          <span class="tag">Arcade Physics</span>
          <span class="tag">Vitest</span>
          <span class="tag">PostMessage SDK</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Project 3: CCT World Engine -->
      <article class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--accent);">Deterministic Simulation & Mechanics</span>
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; margin-top: 0.25rem;">CCT World Engine</h2>
            <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--text);">Astronomical Orbit & Calendar Simulation Engine</p>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center;">
            <a href="https://github.com/pedroivovasconcelos/cct-world-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem; font-size: 0.85rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: var(--surface-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line);">GitHub ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p style="color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          High-precision, pure-Python deterministic celestial mechanics and seasonal simulator for the five-book epic fantasy universe *Correndo Contra o Tempo*. Resolves dual-star orbital barycenters, axial tilt insolation, calendar drift, and planetary phase cycles.
        </p>

        <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);">
          <strong style="display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text);">Architecture & Engineering Highlights:</strong>
          <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-soft); margin: 0;">
            <li><strong>201 Pytest Test Suites:</strong> Strict unit tests verifying Keplerian orbital physics, leap-year calculations, and solar noon angles.</li>
            <li><strong>Deterministic Time Step:</strong> Exact reproducibility across seeds, platform architectures, and time horizons spanning thousands of simulation years.</li>
            <li><strong>Model-Agnostic JSON Export:</strong> Outputs clean canonical ephemeris feeds for 3D renderers, story engines, and interactive world maps.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <span class="tag">Python 3.12</span>
          <span class="tag">Pytest</span>
          <span class="tag">Keplerian Physics</span>
          <span class="tag">Orbital Mechanics</span>
          <span class="tag">Deterministic Math</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Project 4: Dióio Real Estate OS -->
      <article class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--accent);">Real Estate Intelligence</span>
            <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; margin-top: 0.25rem;">Dióio Real Estate OS</h2>
            <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--text);">Multi-City Property Intelligence & Financial Decision Comparator</p>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center;">
            <a href="https://dioio.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem; font-size: 0.85rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: var(--surface-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line);">Production ↗</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/pedroivovasconcelos/dioio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem; font-size: 0.85rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: var(--surface-soft); border: 1px solid var(--line);">GitHub ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p style="color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          Data-driven real estate platform built on Next.js 16 and Supabase. Compares real property acquisition strategies across São Paulo and Curitiba, modeling CAIXA mortgage amortization (SAC/Price) against real estate consortium quotas, opportunity costs, and auction margins.
        </p>

        <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);">
          <strong style="display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text);">Architecture & Engineering Highlights:</strong>
          <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-soft); margin: 0;">
            <li><strong>Audited Financial Decision Models:</strong> Mathematical comparators evaluating inflation (IPCA/INCC), interest spreads, and capital opportunity cost.</li>
            <li><strong>Zero-Leakage Demo Mode:</strong> Isolated sandbox providing realistic sample fixtures for testing and evaluation without connecting to production tables.</li>
            <li><strong>Row-Level Security (RLS):</strong> Granular Supabase security policies protecting private property data and financial profiles.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <span class="tag">Next.js 16</span>
          <span class="tag">Supabase SSR</span>
          <span class="tag">PostgreSQL</span>
          <span class="tag">Financial Modeling</span>
          <span class="tag">Leaflet Maps</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
